ent Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"21 1/2 x 27 1/2 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"extended_medium_description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/extended_medium_description"}],"content":"Pastel on moderately thick, cream, rough paper mounted to a thick grey cardboard; commercially prepared pastel board with a sand-textured surface\n(Source: Paper Survey researched by Judith C. Walsh and published in Lynes, 1999.)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"(An American Place, New York, NY); Elizabeth Arden, New York, NY, 1939; Patricia Graham Young, New York, NY, by 1986; Estate of Patricia Graham Young, 1990; Sotheby's, New York, NY, sale no. 6025, lot no. 230, 24 May 1990; Gerald Peters Gallery, Santa Fe, New Mexico, and Hirschl \u0026 Adler Galleries, Inc., New York, NY, 1990; (Thea Westreich Art Advisory Services, Inc., New York, NY) (Source: Lynes, 1999)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Complete","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_complete"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe. A White Camellia, 1938. Pastel on paper mounted on cardboard, 21 1/2 x 27 1/2 inches. Private Collection. © Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Whitney Archive indicates, \"Sold to Elizabeth Arden.\" Backing inscription dates 1939. Whitney Archive, Downtown Gallery Archive, Abiquiú Notebooks date 1938. Dated 1938 on basis of inclusion in 1939 New York (An American Place) exhibition and Stieglitz–O'Keeffe 